From: Custom TLS Fingerprint <noreply@example.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] content/devtools: add Emulation.setTLSFingerprint CDP command

Extends the DevTools Emulation domain with two new commands:
  • Emulation.setTLSFingerprint  — activate custom TLS ClientHello params
  • Emulation.resetTLSFingerprint — revert to Chromium defaults

The handler converts CDP parameters (or a JA3 string) to a Mojo call on the
TLSFingerprintService bound in the browser process, which propagates to the
network service process.

Files changed:
  third_party/blink/public/devtools_protocol/browser_protocol.pdl
  content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.h
  content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.cc
---
 content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.cc         | 95 +++++++++++++
 content/browser/devtools/protocol/emulation_handler.h          | 10 ++
 third_party/blink/public/devtools_protocol/browser_protocol.pdl| 48 +++++++
 3 files changed, 153 insertions(+)

diff --git a/third_party/blink/public/devtools_protocol/browser_protocol.pdl b/third_party/blink/public/devtools_protocol/browser_protocol.pdl
index aaaabbbb..ccccdddd 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/public/devtools_protocol/browser_protocol.pdl
+++ b/third_party/blink/public/devtools_protocol/browser_protocol.pdl
@@ -2800,4 +2800,41 @@ domain Emulation
       # Allows overriding the automation flag.
       optional boolean enable
 
+  # Sets a custom TLS ClientHello fingerprint for all new connections.
+  # Remains active until resetTLSFingerprint is called or the browser is closed.
+  #
+  # Provide either a `ja3String` for convenience, or individual fields for
+  # precise control. Individual fields take precedence over ja3String values.
+  #
+  # EXPERIMENTAL
+  experimental command setTLSFingerprint
+    parameters
+      # JA3 fingerprint string (convenience input).
+      # Format: "SSLVersion,Ciphers,Extensions,EllipticCurves,PointFormats"
+      # Each field is a '-'-separated list of decimal IANA integers.
+      # GREASE values are automatically stripped.
+      # Example (Chrome 120 / Windows):
+      #   "771,4865-4866-4867-49195-49199-49196-49200-52393-52392-49171-49172-156-157-47-53,
+      #    0-23-65281-10-11-35-16-5-13-18-51-45-43-27-21,29-23-24,0"
+      optional string ja3String
+      # Cipher suite IANA values in preferred order. Overrides ja3String ciphers.
+      optional array of integer cipherSuites
+      # Supported EC group IANA values in preferred order.
+      # Overrides ja3String ellipticCurves.
+      optional array of integer supportedGroups
+      # TLS extension type values in desired ClientHello send order.
+      # Overrides ja3String extensions.
+      optional array of integer extensionOrder
+      # If true, randomly shuffle extension order each connection.
+      # Takes precedence over extensionOrder.
+      optional boolean permuteExtensions
+      # Minimum TLS version.
+      # 769=TLS1.0, 770=TLS1.1, 771=TLS1.2, 772=TLS1.3
+      optional integer minVersion
+      # Maximum TLS version.
+      optional integer maxVersion
+
+  # Resets the TLS fingerprint to Chromium defaults, undoing setTLSFingerprint.
+  # EXPERIMENTAL
+  experimental command resetTLSFingerprint
 
